WEBVTT

1
00:00:01.050 --> 00:00:07.180
This is the mouse pancreatic Islet image, opened in
QuPath zero point seven.

2
00:00:07.360 --> 00:00:12.999
We'll train a pixel classifier to highlight nuclei in
the fluorescence image.

3
00:00:13.179 --> 00:00:19.304
Along the way, we'll inspect the features, review the
prediction against the source,

4
00:00:19.484 --> 00:00:22.578
and reopen the saved model for editing.

5
00:00:22.758 --> 00:00:28.252
Open the Islet image in a QuPath project. In
Extensions,

6
00:00:28.432 --> 00:00:33.327
open CI Pixel Classifier and choose Train classifier.

7
00:00:33.507 --> 00:00:39.786
The workspace puts model settings, training data, and
preview controls side by side.

8
00:00:39.966 --> 00:00:44.221
Its recent settings are remembered in your QuPath
profile.

9
00:00:44.401 --> 00:00:51.480
Use Random trees and Class labels. For this image,
set Downsample to two,

10
00:00:51.660 --> 00:00:57.055
which is one micrometre per classifier pixel at the
image's calibration.

11
00:00:57.235 --> 00:01:01.794
Leave both image channels selected and start with a
scale of one.

12
00:01:01.974 --> 00:01:06.344
New workspaces enable all ten two-dimensional
filters.

13
00:01:07.394 --> 00:01:12.498
In the viewer, zoom in until you can see the
individual blue nuclei.

14
00:01:12.678 --> 00:01:17.543
Create a class named Nucleus in QuPath's Annotations
pane.

15
00:01:17.723 --> 00:01:24.782
Use the ellipse tool to mark a few representative
nuclei, then assign Nucleus to those annotations.

16
00:01:24.962 --> 00:01:28.732
Place each shape well inside a visible boundary.

17
00:01:28.912 --> 00:01:33.782
Create a second class named Background with an
asterisk at the end.

18
00:01:33.962 --> 00:01:40.141
Add small shapes between nuclei and in darker
regions, then assign that class.

19
00:01:40.321 --> 00:01:46.646
The asterisk tells QuPath to skip this class when
creating objects with the usual settings.

20
00:01:46.826 --> 00:01:50.880
Its labelled pixels still help train the classifier.

21
00:01:51.060 --> 00:01:58.344
Choose a mix of examples across the image. Include
some difficult areas around the red signal,

22
00:01:58.524 --> 00:02:02.984
and avoid annotations that cross from one class into
the other.

23
00:02:03.164 --> 00:02:10.369
Training data lists the number of unlocked
annotations in each class. If a class is missing,

24
00:02:10.548 --> 00:02:14.348
check the labels and whether the annotations are
locked.

25
00:02:15.398 --> 00:02:23.268
Choose Train classifier. The pixel counts and
percentages underneath the annotation counts describe

26
00:02:23.448 --> 00:02:27.657
the inputs actually sampled at the selected
resolution.

27
00:02:27.837 --> 00:02:33.386
The pie chart makes it easier to spot a class with
very few sampled pixels.

28
00:02:33.566 --> 00:02:39.881
Two classes can have the same number of annotations
and contribute different numbers of pixels.

29
00:02:40.061 --> 00:02:47.340
Check the class with fewer samples. A few additional
examples from underrepresented parts

30
00:02:47.520 --> 00:02:52.285
of the image can be more helpful than making one
shape much larger.

31
00:02:52.465 --> 00:02:57.494
The chevron in the top right folds the window down
while you're annotating.

32
00:02:57.674 --> 00:03:02.374
It stays in the same place, and the window keeps its
width.

33
00:03:02.554 --> 00:03:06.898
Live Prediction moves into the header while the
window is folded.

34
00:03:07.078 --> 00:03:11.828
Turn it on to retrain after changing the annotations
or settings.

35
00:03:12.008 --> 00:03:16.008
Click the chevron again to restore the full
workspace.

36
00:03:16.188 --> 00:03:21.117
Live Prediction returns to the Preview card with your
selection intact.

37
00:03:21.297 --> 00:03:28.392
The Undo arrow beside Export JSON uses QuPath's Undo
history. On Windows,

38
00:03:28.572 --> 00:03:31.816
Control Z is the keyboard shortcut.

39
00:03:32.866 --> 00:03:40.780
In Preview, leave Show prediction in viewer enabled.
Choose a prediction region and set the opacity

40
00:03:40.960 --> 00:03:44.430
so you can still see the underlying image.

41
00:03:44.610 --> 00:03:52.000
Pick a region that suits the task. You can keep
prediction within annotations while correcting small

42
00:03:52.180 --> 00:03:56.854
areas, or show it throughout the image when checking
the result.

43
00:03:57.034 --> 00:04:04.958
Turn on Compare with source. Drag the divider. The
raw fluorescence remains on the left

44
00:04:05.138 --> 00:04:09.133
and the classifier overlay is visible on the right.

45
00:04:09.313 --> 00:04:16.728
Look for nuclei that disappear under the overlay.
Also look for green predictions covering tissue

46
00:04:16.908 --> 00:04:19.707
where there is no clear nucleus.

47
00:04:19.887 --> 00:04:26.552
If the same mistake occurs in several places, add
examples of that pattern and train again.

48
00:04:26.732 --> 00:04:31.676
Sweep the divider over a different part of the field
to review the change.

49
00:04:32.726 --> 00:04:37.846
Select Show filters under Features to open the native
QuPath preview.

50
00:04:38.026 --> 00:04:44.485
The channel list identifies the image channel,
filter, and scale used to compute each view.

51
00:04:44.665 --> 00:04:52.014
Start with a Gaussian feature. Move or zoom the image
viewer and select Refresh view to update

52
00:04:52.194 --> 00:04:54.879
the region used by the popup.

53
00:04:55.059 --> 00:04:59.604
Switch to a structure tensor feature to see a
different response.

54
00:04:59.784 --> 00:05:04.568
Brightness here shows the computed feature response
at that location.

55
00:05:04.748 --> 00:05:10.192
Open Advanced training settings to find local
normalization and local scale.

56
00:05:10.372 --> 00:05:13.957
These settings affect the features given to the
model.

57
00:05:14.137 --> 00:05:19.236
The same panel contains sampling and feature
preprocessing controls.

58
00:05:19.416 --> 00:05:25.531
Record changes that matter for your project so
someone else can repeat your training setup.

59
00:05:25.711 --> 00:05:31.970
With Random trees selected and principal component
analysis off, choose Importance.

60
00:05:32.150 --> 00:05:37.745
The separate fit ranks the original channel, filter,
and scale combinations.

61
00:05:37.925 --> 00:05:42.304
Select a row and click Show selected filter to
inspect it.

62
00:05:42.484 --> 00:05:48.409
Use the ranking together with the preview and
validation when deciding whether to keep a feature.

63
00:05:49.459 --> 00:05:55.338
To check how training transfers, put other annotated
images into the project.

64
00:05:55.518 --> 00:06:01.483
Use the same class names, and include every class on
at least two images.

65
00:06:01.663 --> 00:06:09.998
In Training data, choose project images. Move the
extra images into the Selected column and select

66
00:06:10.178 --> 00:06:15.422
Apply. The currently open image is included
automatically.

67
00:06:15.602 --> 00:06:23.472
Select Validate. For each fold, the extension fits on
the other selected images and scores

68
00:06:23.652 --> 00:06:26.881
the labelled pixels in the held-out image.

69
00:06:27.061 --> 00:06:33.516
Read across a row in the confusion matrix. The row is
the annotation class,

70
00:06:33.696 --> 00:06:37.895
and the columns show the classes predicted for those
pixels.

71
00:06:38.075 --> 00:06:44.984
Open Class scores for precision, recall, and F one.
For example,

72
00:06:45.164 --> 00:06:51.564
weak nucleus recall means many annotated nucleus
pixels were predicted as another class.

73
00:06:51.744 --> 00:06:59.074
Open By image to see whether one field is harder.
This demonstration uses annotated areas

74
00:06:59.254 --> 00:07:05.858
from the same Islet specimen. Use independent images
to assess a real workflow.

75
00:07:06.038 --> 00:07:12.702
If you imported fitted preprocessing, select Fit new
preprocessing before validation,

76
00:07:12.882 --> 00:07:17.577
so each fold can learn those settings from its own
training images.

77
00:07:18.627 --> 00:07:22.746
Train with the settings and images you want in the
final model.

78
00:07:22.926 --> 00:07:30.206
Enter a classifier name in Save to project and select
Save. Here the name is Islet nuclei.

79
00:07:30.386 --> 00:07:39.506
Use Export JSON for a standalone file. The saved
model uses QuPath's native pixel classifier format

80
00:07:39.686 --> 00:07:43.795
and can be applied using the standard QuPath tools.

81
00:07:43.975 --> 00:07:50.344
Under Extensions, open CI Pixel Classifier and choose
Load classifier.

82
00:07:50.524 --> 00:07:57.484
Select Islet nuclei from the project list, or use
Open JSON to browse to a file.

83
00:07:57.664 --> 00:08:03.328
The loader lets you preview the result and apply
compatible classifiers straight away.

84
00:08:03.508 --> 00:08:07.958
Check that the new image has the same required input
channels.

85
00:08:08.138 --> 00:08:16.102
Select Edit to close the loader and reopen the
training workspace. The supported model, resolution,

86
00:08:16.282 --> 00:08:21.922
channels, filters, and scales are restored from the
classifier.

87
00:08:22.102 --> 00:08:27.362
Check your training annotations and current sampling
options before retraining.

88
00:08:27.542 --> 00:08:34.001
These are managed by the project or workspace,
alongside the fitted model in the JSON.

89
00:08:35.051 --> 00:08:42.496
Use Create objects from the loader or training
workspace. Choose Full image for this exercise.

90
00:08:42.676 --> 00:08:48.165
For a smaller area, select a parent annotation in the
viewer first.

91
00:08:48.345 --> 00:08:54.604
Choose Annotation for editable outlines, or Detection
if that fits your analysis.

92
00:08:54.784 --> 00:08:59.179
Set a minimum object size in the calibrated area
units.

93
00:08:59.359 --> 00:09:03.578
Enable Split objects to make disconnected regions
separate.

94
00:09:03.758 --> 00:09:10.438
Leave the ignored-class option off to create nucleus
objects without creating background objects.

95
00:09:10.618 --> 00:09:16.198
Check the new outlines against the source, especially
where nuclei touch.

96
00:09:16.378 --> 00:09:22.817
Keep the classifier with the project so you can load
it again or use it on another compatible image.

97
00:09:22.997 --> 00:09:29.596
For the installation steps, individual screenshots,
or a copy of the English captions,

98
00:09:29.776 --> 00:09:32.711
return to the guide below this video.
